1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:04,149
“Rohan ‘exceeds’. He’s
in every meeting.”

2
00:00:04,239 --> 00:00:06,499
Kabir asked just one thing…

3
00:00:06,499 --> 00:00:08,309
“And the work, sir?”

4
00:00:08,309 --> 00:00:10,289
Appraisal week. Kabir
shipped the payments fix…

5
00:00:10,289 --> 00:00:11,718
Rohan did the talking in meetings.

6
00:00:11,718 --> 00:00:14,620
So what got rated—
the work, or the face?

7
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:16,600
It’s the halo effect—

8
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:19,390
Thorndike, 1920.
One good impression…

9
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:21,260
spills onto every separate rating.

10
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:22,940
Visibility shines…

11
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:25,980
so ownership, quality,
teamwork— all go up.

12
00:00:25,980 --> 00:00:29,737
Fight it: ‘attitude’.
Stay quiet: ‘meets’ again.

13
00:00:29,737 --> 00:00:34,925
Riya’s third way: a one-page
evidence doc, before calibration.

14
00:00:34,925 --> 00:00:39,522
Kabir wrote: “Sir, before the
rating, please look at three
things…

15
00:00:39,522 --> 00:00:41,340
work, impact, date.”

16
00:00:41,410 --> 00:00:45,892
Chanakya Niti: guṇair uttamatāṁ
yāti, noccair āsana-saṁsthitaḥ.

17
00:00:45,892 --> 00:00:50,792
You rise by qualities, not a high
seat. A crow on a palace top…

18
00:00:50,792 --> 00:00:52,130
doesn’t become Garuda.

19
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:54,916
The meeting room is
just that palace top.

20
00:00:55,036 --> 00:00:58,686
Your move: send the evidence doc…
or wait for the rating?
